Z||000081||Steve Normington||08-27-2001||06:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>I dont get it. lets say 20 and 40, add 40 yrs, shed be 60 and Id be 80 (still 20 yrs apart). to be a 1/4 of my 80 shed have to stay 20. (((owwwww my brain hurts)) so wouldnt 60 be 3/4 of my age???</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>The figures are for the age differential. IE, when you are 40 and she is 20, the differential is 1/2 your age. When you are 80 and she is 60, the differential will be 1/4 of your age.||||reg||1
